{"book":"Titus","chapter":1,"translation":"KJV","url":"/bible/titus/1","verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of Jesus Christ, according to the faith of God’s elect, and the acknowledging of the truth which is after godliness;","words":[["Paul,",["G3972"]],["a servant",["G1401"]],["of God,",["G2316"]],["and",["G1161"]],["an apostle",["G652"]],["of Jesus",["G2424"]],["Christ,",["G5547"]],["according to",["G2596"]],["the faith",["G4102"]],["of God’s elect,",["G1588"]],["and",["G2532"]],["the acknowledging",["G1922"]],["of the truth",["G225"]],["which",["G3588"]],["is after",["G2596"]],["godliness;",[]]]},{"verse":2,"text":"In hope of eternal life, which God, that cannot lie, promised before the world began;","words":[["In",["G1909"]],["hope",["G1680"]],["of eternal",["G166"]],["life,",["G2222"]],["which",["G3739"]],["God,",["G2316"]],["that cannot lie,",["G893"]],["promised",["G1861"]],["before",["G4253"]],["the world",["G166"]],["began;",[]]]},{"verse":3,"text":"But hath in due times manifested his word through preaching, which is committed unto me according to the commandment of God our Saviour;","words":[["But",["G1161"]],["hath",["G5319"]],["in due",["G2398"]],["times",["G2540"]],["manifested",["G5319"]],["his",["G846"]],["word",["G3056"]],["through",["G1722"]],["preaching,",["G2782"]],["which",["G3739"]],["is committed",["G4100"]],["unto me",["G1473"]],["according to",["G2596"]],["the commandment",["G2003"]],["of God",["G2316"]],["our",["G2257"]],["Saviour;",[]]]},{"verse":4,"text":"To Titus, mine own son after the common faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ our Saviour.","words":[["To Titus,",["G5103"]],["mine own",["G1103"]],["son",["G5043"]],["after",["G2596"]],["the common",["G2839"]],["faith:",["G4102"]],["Grace,",["G5485"]],["mercy,",["G1656"]],["and peace,",["G1515"]],["from",["G575"]],["God",["G2316"]],["the Father",["G3962"]],["and",["G2532"]],["the Lord",["G2962"]],["Jesus",["G2424"]],["Christ",["G5547"]],["our",["G2257"]],["Saviour.",[]]]},{"verse":5,"text":"For this cause left I thee in Crete, that thou shouldest set in order the things that are wanting, and ordain elders in every city, as I had appointed thee:","words":[["For this",["G5127"]],["cause",["G5484"]],["left I",["G2641"]],["thee",["G4571"]],["in",["G1722"]],["Crete,",["G2914"]],["that",["G2443"]],["thou shouldest set in order",["G1930"]],["the things that are wanting,",["G3007"]],["and",["G2532"]],["ordain",["G2525"]],["elders",["G4245"]],["in every",["G2596"]],["city,",["G4172"]],["as",["G5613"]],["I",["G1473"]],["had appointed",["G1299"]],["thee:",[]]]},{"verse":6,"text":"If any be blameless, the husband of one wife, having faithful children not accused of riot or unruly.","words":[["If any",["G1536"]],["be",["G2076"]],["blameless,",["G410"]],["the husband",["G435"]],["of one",["G3391"]],["wife,",["G1135"]],["having",["G2192"]],["faithful",["G4103"]],["children",["G5043"]],["not",["G3361"]],["accused",["G1722","G2724"]],["of riot",["G810"]],["or",["G2228"]],["unruly.",[]]]},{"verse":7,"text":"For a bishop must be blameless, as the steward of God; not selfwilled, not soon angry, not given to wine, no striker, not given to filthy lucre;","words":[["For",["G1063"]],["a bishop",["G1985"]],["must",["G1163"]],["be",["G1511"]],["blameless,",["G410"]],["as",["G5613"]],["the steward",["G3623"]],["of God;",["G2316"]],["not",["G3361"]],["selfwilled,",["G829"]],["not",["G3361"]],["soon angry,",["G3711"]],["not",["G3361"]],["given to wine,",["G3943"]],["no",["G3361"]],["striker,",["G4131"]],["not",["G3361"]],["given to filthy lucre;",[]]]},{"verse":8,"text":"But a lover of hospitality, a lover of good men, sober, just, holy, temperate;","words":[["But",["G235"]],["a lover of hospitality,",["G5382"]],["a lover of good men,",["G5358"]],["sober,",["G4998"]],["just,",["G1342"]],["holy,",["G3741"]],["temperate;",[]]]},{"verse":9,"text":"Holding fast the faithful word as he hath been taught, that he may be able by sound doctrine both to exhort and to convince the gainsayers.","words":[["Holding fast",["G472"]],["the faithful",["G4103"]],["word",["G3056"]],["as",["G2596"]],["he hath been taught,",["G1322"]],["that",["G2443"]],["he may be",["G5600"]],["able",["G1415"]],["by",["G1722"]],["sound",["G5198"]],["doctrine",["G1319"]],["both",["G2532"]],["to exhort",["G3870"]],["and",["G2532"]],["to convince",["G1651"]],["the gainsayers.",[]]]},{"verse":10,"text":"For there are many unruly and vain talkers and deceivers, specially they of the circumcision:","words":[["For",["G1063"]],["there are",["G1526"]],["many",["G4183"]],["unruly",["G506"]],["and",["G2532"]],["vain talkers",["G3151"]],["and",["G2532"]],["deceivers,",["G5423"]],["specially",["G3122"]],["they of",["G1537"]],["the circumcision:",[]]]},{"verse":11,"text":"Whose mouths must be stopped, who subvert whole houses, teaching things which they ought not, for filthy lucre’s sake.","words":[["Whose",["G3739"]],["mouths",["G1993"]],["must",["G1163"]],["be stopped,",["G1993"]],["who",["G3748"]],["subvert",["G396"]],["whole",["G3650"]],["houses,",["G3624"]],["teaching",["G1321"]],["things which",["G3739"]],["they ought",["G1163"]],["not,",["G3361"]],["for",["G5484"]],["filthy",["G150"]],["lucre’s sake.",[]]]},{"verse":12,"text":"One of themselves, even a prophet of their own, said, The Cretians are alway liars, evil beasts, slow bellies.","words":[["One",["G5100"]],["of",["G1537"]],["themselves,",["G846"]],["even a prophet",["G4396"]],["of their",["G846"]],["own,",["G2398"]],["said,",["G2036"]],["The Cretians",["G2912"]],["are alway",["G104"]],["liars,",["G5583"]],["evil",["G2556"]],["beasts,",["G2342"]],["slow",["G692"]],["bellies.",[]]]},{"verse":13,"text":"This witness is true. Wherefore rebuke them sharply, that they may be sound in the faith;","words":[["This",["G3778"]],["witness",["G3141"]],["is",["G2076"]],["true.",["G227"]],["Wherefore",["G1223","G3739","G156"]],["rebuke",["G1651"]],["them",["G846"]],["sharply,",["G664"]],["that",["G2443"]],["they may be sound",["G5198"]],["in",["G1722"]],["the faith;",[]]]},{"verse":14,"text":"Not giving heed to Jewish fables, and commandments of men, that turn from the truth.","words":[["Not",["G3361"]],["giving heed",["G4337"]],["to Jewish",["G2451"]],["fables,",["G3454"]],["and",["G2532"]],["commandments",["G1785"]],["of men,",["G444"]],["that turn from",["G654"]],["the truth.",[]]]},{"verse":15,"text":"Unto the pure all things are pure: but unto them that are defiled and unbelieving is nothing pure; but even their mind and conscience is defiled.","words":[["Unto the pure",["G2513"]],["all things",["G3956"]],["are pure:",["G3303","G2513"]],["but",["G1161"]],["unto them that are defiled",["G3392"]],["and",["G2532"]],["unbelieving",["G571"]],["is nothing",["G3762"]],["pure;",["G2513"]],["but",["G235"]],["even",["G2532"]],["their",["G846"]],["mind",["G3563"]],["and",["G2532"]],["conscience",["G4893"]],["is defiled.",[]]]},{"verse":16,"text":"They profess that they know God; but in works they deny him, being abominable, and disobedient, and unto every good work reprobate.","words":[["They profess",["G3670"]],["that they know",["G1492"]],["God;",["G2316"]],["but",["G1161"]],["in works",["G2041"]],["they deny",["G720"]],["him, being",["G5607"]],["abominable,",["G947"]],["and",["G2532"]],["disobedient,",["G545"]],["and",["G2532"]],["unto",["G4314"]],["every",["G3956"]],["good",["G18"]],["work",["G2041"]],["reprobate.",[]]]}]}